},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Imperial forces led by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Juno Eclipse"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Juno_Eclipse","referenceId":"reference:1afda9bb6f5c2327"}," assaulted the planet after the Empire discovered evidence that the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Callosians"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Callosians?action=edit&redlink=1"}," were developing a new offensive technology intended to oppose those who were spreading the New Order.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["15\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["The Imperial bombardment destroyed much of the planet's lush surface and sent the formerly fertile environment into a permanent winter that killed anything that survived the initial assault. Though the atmosphere remains breathable, incessant ice storms and subfreezing temperatures prevent any permanent habitation.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["20\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Callosians"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Callosians?action=edit&redlink=1"}," who were away from the planet at the time of the bombardment defied logic and returned to their devastated homeworld, presumably to die.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["25\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Imperial surveys that returned later found no life signs on the planet's surface and no evidence of survivor enclaves.\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Social Sciences"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DC\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["RESULT\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["The reclusive ",{"tag":"a","children":["Callosians"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Callosians?action=edit&redlink=1"}," d